### **3. SCSS Styling Rules (from `resource/scss/pages/_main.scss`)**

**File**: `c:\Users\edn_y\renew_nineonelabs\resource\scss\pages\_main.scss`  
**Lines**: 469–569

```scss
.no-main-story {
  width: 100%;

  &__inner {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    margin-top: var(--header-height);
  }

  &__body {
    width: 100%;
  }

  &__content {
    @include flex-center();                    // Flexbox center
    flex-direction: column;                    // Stacked vertically

    @include mq(md) {
      align-items: flex-start;                // Mobile: left-align
    }

    .block {
      width: 50%;                             // Default: 50% width
      padding-bottom: var(--gutter-4xl);

      &.left {
        margin-left: auto;                    // Push left block to right side
      }

      &.right {
        margin-right: auto;                   // Would push right block to left side
        width: 72%;                           // If right block exists, wider
        padding-bottom: var(--gutter-4xl);
        padding-top: var(--gutter-3xl);
        position: relative;
      }

      // Breakpoint: Large (lg)
      @include mq(lg) {
        width: 64%;

        &.right {
          width: 84%;
        }
      }

      // Breakpoint: Medium (md) — Mobile
      @include mq(md) {
        width: 100%;
        padding-bottom: var(--gutter-2xl);

        &.left,
        &.right {
          width: 100%;
          margin-left: 0;
          margin-right: 0;
        }

        &.right {
          padding-top: 0;
          padding-bottom: var(--gutter-2xl);
        }
      }

      .title {
        h4 {
          margin-top: var(--gutter-xs);
        }
      }

      .body {
        margin-top: var(--gutter-lg);

        p {
          margin-top: var(--gutter-sm);
        }
      }
    }

    // Secondary text area
    .etc {
      width: 45%;                             // Smaller width
      margin-left: auto;                      // Right-aligned

      @include mq(md) {
        width: 100%;
        margin-left: 0;                       // Full-width on mobile
      }

      .--divider {
        margin-top: fluid(6, 14);
      }

      p {
        display: flex;
        gap: var(--gutter-2xs);

        @include mq(sm) {
          flex-direction: column;             // Stack divider + text on small screens
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

**Key observations**:
- **Responsive layout**: Desktop uses 50% width blocks with margins; mobile collapses to 100% full-width
- **Left-aligned block**: `.block.left` uses `margin-left: auto` to push it right
- **Right-block support**: Styles exist for `.block.right` (not currently used), with 72% width (lg: 84%)
- **`.etc` supplementary**: Always right-aligned with smaller width (45%), flex layout with divider

